1
00:00:00,06 --> 00:00:02,02
- [Instructor] The Recoil API is very similar

2
00:00:02,02 --> 00:00:03,05
to the React useState Hook,

3
00:00:03,05 --> 00:00:05,07
except that it takes a RecoilState instead

4
00:00:05,07 --> 00:00:07,03
of a default value as arguments.

5
00:00:07,03 --> 00:00:10,02
So let's see how it works.

6
00:00:10,02 --> 00:00:12,00
We're going to see an example right here.

7
00:00:12,00 --> 00:00:13,05
So you're going to make sure that you add

8
00:00:13,05 --> 00:00:16,05
to the scope of your projects, useRecoilState,

9
00:00:16,05 --> 00:00:17,08
and the way that you define it,

10
00:00:17,08 --> 00:00:21,09
it's going to be very similar to the React's useState.

11
00:00:21,09 --> 00:00:23,03
So instead here,

12
00:00:23,03 --> 00:00:24,05
instead of the default value,

13
00:00:24,05 --> 00:00:28,02
it's going to be the atom that we have defined earlier.

14
00:00:28,02 --> 00:00:30,05
And it's going to be the same as with useState.

15
00:00:30,05 --> 00:00:32,05
It's going to return an array

16
00:00:32,05 --> 00:00:37,04
with the first element being the current value of the state.

17
00:00:37,04 --> 00:00:39,07
And the second element is the setup function

18
00:00:39,07 --> 00:00:41,04
that we use to update the value

19
00:00:41,04 --> 00:00:44,01
of the given state when it is called.

20
00:00:44,01 --> 00:00:46,09
And so this hook useRecoilState will subscribe

21
00:00:46,09 --> 00:00:47,07
to the components,

22
00:00:47,07 --> 00:00:51,07
will subscribe to the state, which is contains in the atom,

23
00:00:51,07 --> 00:00:53,01
so the component re-renders

24
00:00:53,01 --> 00:00:56,06
for any change in the requested states.

25
00:00:56,06 --> 00:00:58,06
So let's go back to our startup project.

26
00:00:58,06 --> 00:01:01,03
Here the goal will be to replace the current useState

27
00:01:01,03 --> 00:01:04,02
that we have listed inside the App component.

28
00:01:04,02 --> 00:01:05,09
So we have several of them.

29
00:01:05,09 --> 00:01:08,06
And instead, we're going to use the hook useRecoilStates

30
00:01:08,06 --> 00:01:11,07
to subscribe to the state, which are contained in atoms.

31
00:01:11,07 --> 00:01:13,06
And so this will allow to read

32
00:01:13,06 --> 00:01:16,00
and update the state with useRecoilState,

33
00:01:16,00 --> 00:01:18,00
which has a similar syntax of the useState.

34
00:01:18,00 --> 00:01:20,02
So we don't need to change much right here.

35
00:01:20,02 --> 00:01:23,06
First, we just need to make sure that we add to the scope.

36
00:01:23,06 --> 00:01:26,06
So useRecoilState like so.

37
00:01:26,06 --> 00:01:29,08
Let's go back to inside the App component.

38
00:01:29,08 --> 00:01:32,09
We're going to replace here with useRecoilState.

39
00:01:32,09 --> 00:01:35,03
And instead of adding a default value,

40
00:01:35,03 --> 00:01:38,02
we're going to specify the atom that we have defined,

41
00:01:38,02 --> 00:01:41,05
which will be in this case listState.

42
00:01:41,05 --> 00:01:47,00
Let's do the same for this variable.

43
00:01:47,00 --> 00:01:53,06
And here it's going to be the atom allStates.

44
00:01:53,06 --> 00:01:59,05
For isFiltered, it's going to be filterState.

45
00:01:59,05 --> 00:02:02,04
And there is one last, which is inputValue.

46
00:02:02,04 --> 00:02:05,04
So I'm going to go ahead and add this one right here.

47
00:02:05,04 --> 00:02:09,02
And that's going to be useRecoilStates

48
00:02:09,02 --> 00:02:14,01
and it's going to be inputValue like so.

49
00:02:14,01 --> 00:02:15,03
So that's done for this part.

50
00:02:15,03 --> 00:02:19,09
You can see that now we've been able to subscribe

51
00:02:19,09 --> 00:02:22,07
to the states, which are contained in Atom.

52
00:02:22,07 --> 00:02:24,08
So this is very simple, a very simple process

53
00:02:24,08 --> 00:02:27,00
because the syntax is very similar

54
00:02:27,00 --> 00:02:30,05
to the useState hook from the React API.

55
00:02:30,05 --> 00:02:33,05
Next, we see how to create derived data

56
00:02:33,05 --> 00:02:36,00
from the state with selectors.

